# Concurrency: MAX_WORKERS

RULE: Set MAX_WORKERS based on workload type and monitor RAM. Never hardcode worker counts without type-based rationale.
WHY: Wrong worker counts cause OOM kills (CPU-bound with 16 workers) or underutilization (I/O-bound with 1 worker).
CODEX: 04-architecture/concurrency.md

Batch mode (parallel dates):
  I/O-bound (GCS read/write, API calls): MAX_WORKERS = 16
  CPU-bound (feature calculation, ML inference): MAX_WORKERS = 1–3

Live mode (parallel venues):
  One thread per WebSocket connection (never share a WebSocket across threads)

Adaptive RAM thresholds (required for all batch workers):
  85% RAM → reduce active workers by 50%
  90% RAM → emergency shutdown of non-critical workers
  Monitor via: psutil.virtual_memory().percent

DO:
  MAX_WORKERS = config.max_workers  # from UnifiedCloudConfig field
  with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=MAX_WORKERS) as executor: ...

NEVER:
  ThreadPoolExecutor()  # no max_workers limit
  Hardcode max_workers=16 for CPU-bound workloads
  Share WebSocket connections across threads
